2. **Per-BFS-step normalization** at line 59: `normalizePath(importer.file)` is called for every node traversed. These `importer.file` values come from the builder (un-normalized on Windows), so this is real repeated work.

3. **No Windows-specific test coverage**: All tests use Unix-style paths, so the `Map.get()` direct lookup always succeeds and the new fallback path (lines 14–18) — the actual Windows fix — is never exercised.

4. `changedFile` passed into `findAffectedStoryFiles` is already normalized by the call site in `buildStatuses()` (lines 247, 250 use `normalizePath`), so the `normalizePath(changedFile)` at line 29 is redundant but harmless defensive coding.

